Release Notes AM335x-PD17.1.0
=============================
 
- Linux Kernel v4.4.52
- barebox 2017.06.1
- Yocto 2.2.1 (morty)
- Qt 5.7
 
Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
 
 - phytec-qt5demo-image
 
Build Environment:
------------------
 
 - Ubuntu 16.04 64Bit
 
New Configuration:
------------------
 
- Added support for new machine:
       * phyboard-regor-am335x-2
       * phycore-emmc-am335x-1
 
 
New Features:
-------------
       * Add support for EMMC
 
Known Issues:
-------------
 
 - phycore-am335x-som / phycore-r2-am335x-som: 
        * Boot tests showed in about 2 of 2000 boots that the SMSC LAN8710 phy could not be found.
          The PHY ID readout is wrong. The generic PHY driver will take over. Ethernet is still
          functional in this case.
 
 - phycore-am335x/phycore-r2-am335x:
        * rtc1 (AM335x RTC) has high deviation
 
 - CAN tests with 20kbit/s did not run successfully. All other CANopen standard bit rates are
   working. This can be fixed by switching the clock from 25 to 24 Mhz, but new problems with
   other components can occur.

 - The Yocto SDK build process will fail, becaus there are missing dependencies.
 
Notes:
------
 
 - New AC158 display is now standard.
